{"timestamp": "2025-07-29T02:16:11.987028", "function_name": "collect", "function_body": "  # Mapping from direction strings to action indices\n  dir_to_action = {\"UP\": 0, \"DOWN\": 1, \"LEFT\": 2, \"RIGHT\": 3}\n\n  # Get the index of the primitive we want to collect\n  primitive_index = env.world.cookbook.index[primitive]\n\n  # Initialize list to store actions\n  actions = []\n\n  # Get initial state and grid\n  current_state = env._current_state\n  grid = current_state.grid\n\n  # Width and height of the grid\n  width, height = grid.shape[:2]\n\n  # Agent's starting position\n  start_pos = current_state.pos\n\n  # Search for the primitive in a simple BFS manner\n  queue = [start_pos]\n  visited = set()\n  parent = {}\n\n  while queue:\n      pos = queue.pop(0)\n      if pos in visited:\n          continue\n      visited.add(pos)\n\n      x, y = pos\n      # Check if the current position has the primitive\n      if grid[x, y, primitive_index] > 0:\n          # Backtrack to get the path to this position\n          path = []\n          while pos != start_pos:\n              path.append(parent[pos])\n              pos = parent[pos]\n          path.reverse()\n          break\n\n      # Explore neighbors (UP, DOWN, LEFT, RIGHT)\n      for dx, dy, direction in [(-1, 0, \"UP\"), (1, 0, \"DOWN\"), (0, -1, \"LEFT\"), (0, 1, \"RIGHT\")]:\n          nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n          if 0 <= nx < width and 0 <= ny < height:\n              queue.append((nx, ny))\n              parent[(nx, ny)] = direction\n\n  # Convert path directions to actions\n  for direction in path:\n      actions.append(dir_to_action[direction])\n\n  return actions", "island_id": 7, "scores": {"3": -1}}
